If you're thinking of the 'sound' option, that "has nothing to do with
your computer's audio capabilities"; it's purely for filtering messages
about in-game sounds.

> I also remember several years ago a programme that added sound into
> nethack.  It stored .WAV's in your NH directory, and played them based
> on text appearing in your message box.  So if it said "you zap the
> magic missile" it would play a corresponding file.  I also think you
> could add your own .WAV's and define when they were used.
> 
> Is this still available?  Even better, has anybody refined this, or
> used other techniques to get sound FX into NH?

This has been replaced by (or incorporated into, I'm not sure) the
SOUND system; read section 9.7 of the Guidebook.

(If you can't get that working, under one of the platforms that's
supposed to be supported, come back to us with how it failed.)

